{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Philosopher: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja63'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 63 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Itthivagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Women </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>3. Takkapaṇḍitajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Philosopher: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Kodhanā akataññū ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Hateful ingrates! </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>pisuṇā mittabhedikā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Slanderous traitors! </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Brahmacariyaṁ cara bhikkhu, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Live the spiritual life, mendicant, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>so sukhaṁ na vihāhasīti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>you will not be bereft of happiness. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Takkapaṇḍitajātakaṁ tatiyaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
